ner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":340613,"name":"The Wife","image_path":"/6cGJlTPOICAi4KfMmAVe6r7Oh1s.jpg","director":"Björn Runge","winner":false}}]},{"type":"block_special","title":"Host","description":"On December 4, 2018, it was announced that Kevin Hart would host the ceremony. At the time, Hart expressed how honored and excited he was by the invitation to host. Controversy began when old comments and jokes made by Hart surfaced containing slurs and homophobic language. After Hart refused to apologize on the matter, on December 6 he ruled out hosting the Oscars, saying he did not want to be a public \"distraction\" for the ceremony.<br/><br/>\n\nOn January 9, 2019, it was reported that the Academy was planning to hold the ceremony without a host, choosing instead to invite a series of presenters for the various segments and the presentation of awards in the various categories. If this scenario materialized, it would be the first time the ceremony had no main host since the 1989 Oscars. Previous hosts such as Seth MacFarlane, Ellen DeGeneres, Neil Patrick Harris, Chris Rock and Jimmy Kimmel showed no interest in hosting the ceremony again. Finally, on February 5, 2019, the Academy announced, through a spokesperson and without giving further details, that the ceremony would not have a main host."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Supporting Actor","nominee_list":[{"type":"person","id":932967,"image_path":"/y9mf12rlZBlVJS6JYuCPpjTaLT6.jpg","name":"Mahershala Ali","winner":true,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":490132,"name":"Green Book","image_path":"/jaosA7NFPYBDueQ3X3SkADN6aS.jpg","director":"Peter Farrelly","winner":true}},{"type":"person","id":6807,"image_path":"/4zjUldl3ykbgcLO7FxWppR6s7Ck.jpg","name":"Sam Rockwell","winner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":429197,"name":"Vice","image_path":"/n1XcudR8wfo7KMtJ7eygAyEkJLx.jpg","director":"Adam McKay","winner":false}},{"type":"person","id":1023139,"image_path":"/fsbGQ1eZFgdsG1XnKlhNSvHsiGo.jpg","name":"