rfcdoRa6jTAnA.jpg","director":"Ryan Coogler","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":369972,"name":"First Man","image_path":"/bRQ0CKECt5B3aE8YqW9r6DvaxRY.jpg","director":"Damien Chazelle","winner":false}]},{"type":"block_special","title":"Categories presented during commercial breaks","description":"In order to shorten the ceremony's television broadcast, the Academy announced on February 11, 2019, that four categories (Best Cinematography, Best Live Action Short Film, Best Film Editing and Best Makeup and Hairstyling) would be presented during commercial breaks. However, the Oscar presentations in those categories would be streamed online through the official website, and the winners' speeches would be aired later in the ceremony. After some backlash, notably from some of the professionals nominated in those categories, the Academy reversed the decision four days later and announced that all 24 categories would be presented during the live broadcast of the ceremony. <br/><br/>\n\nThis edition's television broadcast was expected to last three hours, with an estimated 90 seconds allotted to each winner (or winners) in the various categories, from the moment the names are announced until they take the stage and finish their acceptance speech. The ceremony's broadcast ended up lasting 3 hours and 23 minutes, the shortest since 2012."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Visual Effects","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":369972,"name":"First Man","image_path":"/bRQ0CKECt5B3aE8YqW9r6DvaxRY.jpg","director":"Damien Chazelle","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":299536,"name":"Avengers: Infinity War","image_path":"/89QTZmn34iwXYeCpVxhC9UrT8sX.jpg","director":"Joe Russo e Anthony Russo","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":333339,"name":"Ready Player One","image_path":"/sN46sgCsWqwgHMu4mEtKJ19knVr.jpg","director":"Ernest Cline","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":348350,"name":"Solo: A Star Wars Story","image_path":"/jAMEX0syUh6sbjBiysibzrFpbo.jpg","director":"Ron Howard",